testing='''<div class="callout"><strong>First test goal:</strong> distinguish “could not infer the answer” from “could not read or operate the prop.” Do not use completion alone as proof that every gate is fair.</div>
<div class="grid">'''+panel('For two players','<p>Let each player own one Rollo task and one Harald branch, then compare. They can alternate reading/navigation on Aud. Use two maps at a time in the finale; keep the journal available to both. No simultaneous timing or dexterity requirement should demand a third person.</p>')+panel('For four players','<p>Use two pairs during Rollo and Harald. Rotate reader, mapper, counter and lock-handler so one confident solver does not monopolize the bag. Four maps give the finale its best team moment; bring the group together to justify the final order.</p>')+'''</div>
<h3 style="margin-top:24px">Physical proof before a cold team</h3><ol class="testlist"><li><strong>Print and trim:</strong> 5×3.5-inch cards, Letter maps, actual ticket sizes. Confirm both sides match. Count 22 cards. Check R1’s two tiny bolts and R6’s three boars without telling the tester the counts.</li><li><strong>Light puzzles:</strong> L2/L3 must reveal 1576 through the final stock. The mirrored ticket must reconstruct I–K while the stain still hides the original. The map’s reverse must not obscure the ticket signal. Test at ordinary table lighting.</li><li><strong>Aud route:</strong> walk every leg from the printed directions, separately recording bridge/ford/gate crossings. Check the alternate village branch. Make a marked operator answer image from the actual sheet; the existing ANSWER PDF shows the final seven, not the treasure-route solution.</li><li><strong>Weight:</strong> use the final scale and coin set. Repeat zeroing and weighing; verify the selected pile always gives the intended four retained digits and other piles do not. Match the cache and coin symbol; do not rely on knowing which pile the designer meant.</li><li><strong>Board:</strong> rebuild from the two papers with no help. Confirm exactly 16 dark, 6 light and one king. Check that all players follow the printed house rules and can count 2/5/3.</li><li><strong>Final shapes:</strong> hide ANSWER headings and expected digits. Ask someone unfamiliar with the game to identify the four north-up traced routes, then test incorrect routes including decoys. Record what they actually read. Do not prompt “does this look like a 2?”</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong> test each combination, all needed letters and all closures. Check that both Rollo locks are necessary, the cryptex contains its key and no needed card is packed behind itself.</li></ol>
<h3>Cold playtest: one pair, then one group of four</h3><p>Use people who have not read this page. Give only the opening materials and hint access. An observer may silently record problems, but should not supply missing rules; any intervention becomes a failed self-guided gate for that run.</p>'''+table(['Record','Why it matters'],[
('Start/end and each gate opened','Measure total elapsed time and where delays occur.'),('Hints opened and exact point of confusion','Separate discovery, interpretation, manipulation and validation issues.'),('Alternative plausible answers','Ambiguity is not solved by a lock rejecting one guess.'),('Who has something useful to do','Watch prolonged idle players, especially during Aud and board setup.'),('Every spoken instruction from an observer','These must move onto props or the optional hint system.'),('Recognition of all four digits without the answer','The finale must deliver its own payoff.'),('Packing/reset errors and visible answers','Test the kit as it will actually be reused.')])+'''
<h3>Acceptance for a first playable version</h3><p>Both team sizes finish without unplanned host intervention, every mandatory gate has sufficient in-game evidence, intended physical readings are repeatable, hints are reachable, and all four final digits are recognized. Measure whether elapsed time falls in the 60–90-minute goal. A slow or incomplete run is useful evidence; record the cause before cutting puzzles.</p>
<h3>Optional hints</h3><p><a href="'''+R+'''Norse_Hints_Review.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open separate review hint page →</a>. Eleven topic-based gates; three progressive hints plus a closed solution for each. It is a local prototype, not a published service. Do not send players to this spoiler-filled brainstorm page.</p>
<details><summary>Reset procedure</summary><div><ol><li>Recover all 22 cards, four maps, four museum tickets, two tags, three travel tickets and journal.</li><li>Wipe maps; replace used tally paper; check stock and overlays for damage.</li><li>Count board pieces, sort/restore coin inventory, check scale zero and battery.</li><li>Set and test all locks while open. Never discover a mis-set lock during the next game.</li><li>Repack from the end backward using S0–S8. Photograph the packet contents; keep answer keys outside the bag.</li><li>Restore the cryptex key, close both Rollo locks and verify the opening kit is the only accessible material.</li><li>Reset hint-page disclosures by reloading; verify its availability on the actual player device.</li></ol></div></details>
'''

